{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR RULING (2026-08-22, recorded before implementation): approved scope is ONLY option 1 from the post-3d57 assessment comment — make the per-write enrich-drain gate check an EXISTENCE-ONLY O(1) probe ('is anything pending?') instead of walking the O(backlog) pending-enrichment queue (standing backlog ~1,046 entries prices every tracker write at ~2-8s; this very claim paid a 7375.8 ms gate check). Options 2 (LLM outside the lock / dedicated-clone drain) and 3 (age-out policy for the standing backlog) are NOT in scope — option 2 is under separate design. Do not restructure drain execution or change what gets drained. The gate's DECISION semantics must be preserved: it answers the same yes/no it answers today, just without enumerating the backlog. This ruling is the AC1 'recorded decision on the gate contract': existence-only probe, rationale = cheapest fix that removes the per-write O(backlog) tax while staying marker-fast when quiet; drain throughput/lock-hold and backlog policy remain open under the option-2 design ticket (see 9c72 relates_to)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787446238588227001,"uuid":"7953afda-42d7-4339-a70b-0882afb87897"}